  Parameters: {"utf8"=>"✓", "authenticity_token"=>"634sojT1XmdaXUGxAJJmc9f1sAyZqcJLZUyhKhcbS3g=", "issue"=>{"is_private"=>"0", "project_id"=>"9", "tracker_id"=>"4", "subject"=>"Alpha Site | Sub Account is still able to update downline after being removed all permission", "description"=>"<p><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><strong>I. Incident&nbsp;summary</strong></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p>Related to this topic :&nbsp;http://ccs.starixsoft.com/viewtopic.php?f=335&amp;t=9749</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Sub Account still is able to update downline after being removed all permission</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><strong>II. Incident Details</strong>&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong>Scenario 2 (Pending) : Sub Account still is able to update downline after being removed all permission</strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>1. Login to Alpha as sub-account A (Sub-account A has permission to update setting downline)</p>\r\n\r\n<p>2. In other browser use Main account remove permission of Sub-account A.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>3. Sub-account A still is able to update setting of his downline.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>This bug happen because we get permission of user only one time, after login. If user doesn&#39;t re-login, he will keep his permmision although his permmision was updated by main account (or admin).<br />\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(255, 0, 0)\">Target launch Date: not decided yet due to the technical issues</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#000000\"><strong>Solution</strong>: Eachtime permission of SubAccount is updated, SubAccount will be kicked out and he will receive the latest permission when he/she logs in back.</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p><span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><strong>III. Chronological Order of Events</strong>&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n\r\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"width:500px\">\r\n\t<tbody>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td><strong>Date &amp; Time (GMT+8)</strong></td>\r\n\t\t\t<td><strong>Description &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</strong></td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align:center\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align:center\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align:center\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align:center\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t\t<tr>\r\n\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align:center\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n\t\t</tr>\r\n\t</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n", "status_id"=>"4", "priority_id"=>"3", "assigned_to_id"=>"190", "start_date"=>"2016-10-28", "due_date"=>"2016-12-06", "custom_field_values"=>{"8"=>["N/A", ""], "3"=>["Credit-Alpha", ""], "23"=>["Desktop", ""], "4"=>["Application", ""], "19"=>"N/A", "15"=>"", "7"=>"Permission setting for subaccount is stored on session to prevent hug traffic to DB. Because the function is not used much, it isn't worth requesting data each time user updates permission.\r\n", "17"=>"N/A", "16"=>"We will kick out subaccount. When he/she re-login, he/she will get the new permission."}, "notes"=>"", "private_notes"=>"0", "lock_version"=>"3"}, "issue_template"=>"", "last_journal_id"=>"371", "commit"=>"Submit", "id"=>"61"}
